    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18748" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχόρευτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not trained in the
			dance</i> or <i>chorus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				654a
			</span></i>; <i>not joining in the dance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				44.125
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not attended with the dance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Musae.
					274
				</span></i>
			; esp. in bad sense, <i>ill suiting it, joyless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνείδη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1069
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					121
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Telest.
					1.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
